# Keeps the build context small. Railway (and any remote builder) uploads this
# context before the first line of the Dockerfile runs, so excluding the
# frontend and git history here is the difference between a fast deploy and a
# slow one.
#
# Careful: apps/api, database/ and apps/api/tests MUST stay included. The
# Dockerfile copies the first two, and database/seed/demo_environment.py reads
# a recorded snapshot out of apps/api/tests/fixtures at runtime.

.git
.github

# The API image has no use for the frontend.
apps/web

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite

# Secrets never belong in an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/*.egg-info

**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode

docs
